====Preposition====
{{en-head|prep}}

# In the [[direction]] of; [[towards]].
#: {{ux|en|She looked '''to''' the heavens.}}
# {{non-gloss|Indicating destination or final position:}} In the [[direction]] of, so as to [[arrive]] at or reach.
#: {{ux|en|We are walking '''to''' the shop.}}
#: {{ux|en|The water came right '''to''' the top of this wall.}}
#: {{ux|en|The coconut fell '''to''' the ground.}}
#: {{ux|en|The convention roared as the president stepped '''to''' the podium.}}
#* {{RQ:en:New York Times|date=September 28 2013|author=w:Kenan Malik|title=London Is Special, but Not That Special|url=http://www.nytimes.com/2013/09/29/opinion/sunday/london-is-special-but-not-that-special.html?ref=opinion|accessdate=28 September 2013
|passage=Driven by a perceived political need to adopt a hard-line stance, Mr. Cameron’s coalition government has imposed myriad new restrictions, the aim of which is to reduce net migration '''to''' Britain to below 100,000.}}
# {{non-gloss|Used to indicate the target or recipient of an action.}}
#: {{ux|en|I gave the book '''to''' him.}}
#: {{ux|en|I spoke '''to''' him earlier.}}
#: {{ux|en|He devoted himself '''to''' education.}}
#: {{ux|en|They drank '''to''' his health.}}
# So as to contact, press against, impact, etc.
#: {{ux|en|I fixed the notice '''to''' the wall.}}
#: {{ux|en|Put your shoulder '''to''' the door.}}
#: {{ux|en|To clutch/clasp/hold/press one's hanky '''to''' one's mouth/nose/forehead.}}
# So as to become or reach: {{n-g|indicating a terminal state resulting from an action}}.
#: {{ux|en|His face was beaten '''to''' a pulp.}}
#: {{ux|en|I sang my baby '''to''' sleep.}}
#: {{ux|en|Whisk the mixture '''to''' a smooth consistency.}}
# So as to bring about or elicit (an effect or outcome).
#: {{ux|en|He made several bad-taste jokes '''to''' groans from the audience.}}
#: {{ux|en|I tried complaining, but it was '''to''' no effect.}}
#: {{ux|en|'''To''' everyone's great relief, the tuneless carol singers finally ceased their warbling.}}
# {{non-gloss|Used after an adjective to indicate its application.}}
#: {{ux|en|similar '''to''' ...'', ''relevant '''to''' ...'', ''pertinent '''to''' ...'', ''I was nice '''to''' him'', ''he was cruel '''to''' her'', ''I am used '''to''' walking.}}
# {{non-gloss|Indicating a degree or level reached.}}
#: {{ux|en|It was '''to''' a large extent true.}}
#: {{ux|en|We manufacture these parts '''to''' a very high tolerance.}}
#: {{ux|en|This gauge is accurate '''to''' a second.}}
#: {{ux|en|My car does 25 miles '''to''' the gallon.}}
